# Project Structure Guide

## Overview
This repository is a **Rust workspace** that implements an IPC client library for Microsoft's TypeScript-Go project (**tsgo**).  Most of the code lives under `crates/`, while the upstream `tsgo/` project is included as a *submodule* only for integration testing.

```
./                    ── workspace root (this repo)
├─ Cargo.toml         ── workspace definition
├─ crates/            ── first-party Rust crates (your code)
├─ tests/             ── cross-crate integration tests (need `tsgo` binary)
├─ type-runner/       ── secondary Rust workspace for type-checking benches
├─ tsgo/              ── **third-party** TypeScript-Go implementation (do **not** modify)
└─ scripts/           ── helper scripts (bench fixture generation, etc.)
```

## 1. Rust Workspace – `crates/`
Each sub-directory inside `crates/` is an *independent* crate and a member of the top-level workspace declared in [Cargo.toml](mdc:Cargo.toml).

| Crate | Path | Purpose |
|-------|------|---------|
| **tsgo-client** | [`crates/tsgo-client`](mdc:crates/tsgo-client) | High-level IPC client API exposed to users |
| **tsgo-decoder** | [`crates/tsgo-decoder`](mdc:crates/tsgo-decoder) | Decodes binary AST buffers that come back from `tsgo` |
| **tsgo-transport** | [`crates/tsgo-transport`](mdc:crates/tsgo-transport) | Transport layer abstraction (spawn process / send msgpack) |
| **tsgo-vfs** | [`crates/tsgo-vfs`](mdc:crates/tsgo-vfs) | In-memory virtual file system used by the client |
| **tsgo-rust-ipc** | [`crates/tsgo-rust-ipc`](mdc:crates/tsgo-rust-ipc) | Umbrella crate that re-exports the above pieces |
| **typescript-ast** | [`crates/typescript-ast`](mdc:crates/typescript-ast) | Generated Rust representation of the TypeScript AST enums |

### Decoder test fixtures
`tsgo-decoder` ships ~13 k fixtures:
- Encoded binary: [`tests/fixtures/encoded`](mdc:crates/tsgo-decoder/tests/fixtures/encoded)
- Expected dump: [`tests/fixtures/dumps/go`](mdc:crates/tsgo-decoder/tests/fixtures/dumps/go)

These files are large and checked in with **LF** endings (see `.gitattributes`).

## 2. Cross-crate Tests – `tests/`
- [`tests/integration_tests.rs`](mdc:tests/integration_tests.rs) spins up the `tsgo` binary and performs end-to-end requests.
- Compilation of this crate is gated behind feature flags in CI so it is excluded on Windows & macOS.

## 3. Third-party Submodule – `tsgo/`
`tsgo/` mirrors the official Microsoft repo and is only required for:
1. Building the **`tsgo` binary** (`npx hereby build`)
2. Supplying fixtures / baseline files

> 📢 **Never** edit code in `tsgo/`; upstream changes are pulled via `git submodule update`.

## 4. Helper Scripts
- [`scripts/generate-bench-fixtures/`](mdc:scripts/generate-bench-fixtures) – Go program to regenerate benchmark fixtures.

## 5. Common Commands
```bash
# Build all first-party crates
cargo build --workspace

# Run *unit* tests (no tsgo)
cargo test --workspace --exclude tsgo-rust-ipc-integration-tests

# Run integration tests (requires tsgo binary)
cd tsgo && npm ci && npx hereby build && cd ..
TSGO_PATH=./tsgo/built/local/tsgo \
  cargo test -p tsgo-rust-ipc-integration-tests
```

---
Use this guide to quickly locate code and understand ownership boundaries between **your Rust crates** and the **upstream tsgo project**.
